#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Over a Surface as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10279bac-75c2-5820-bf33-84359cbf720e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} {:answer/id #uuid "397e53f3-63a0-518a-999e-8c3d8631bb27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275987} {:answer/id #uuid "897e0260-ef83-5fe5-9ee2-95ed9d4cd1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7u+8v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276718} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3f2f9b-ef08-5972-b94d-02717ccd84df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277162} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6d4a87-66ae-58b1-806a-631ade59590d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u-8v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10279bac-75c2-5820-bf33-84359cbf720e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} :answer-field/id #uuid "8692e3d1-c9bd-5cca-9274-6af9e13d6963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bf481ef-95d3-5b3f-b324-29ecd57febda" :question/math-academy-id "q-161358" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=3x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 5$ and $-3\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 5,\\,-3\\le v\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u-2v,\\,-v,\\,2u⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-2v)\\cdot (-3)+(-v)\\cdot (2)+2u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+6v-2v+2u \\\\  & =-7u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,-y,\\,2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(-7u+4v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Over a Surface as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9d8774c-14c0-5481-9a1f-1c3acd63867a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} + v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194292} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ce5f03-88a7-5102-bfd3-b0e4a75a4aed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} - v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194293} {:answer/id #uuid "31b2be0c-93a0-5cd7-8143-0596b46129e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} + uv + v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194294} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce44ca0-320e-5c90-a723-d02a6010576d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194295} {:answer/id #uuid "7423bf6e-47f3-548e-afbe-feee4e861dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u + v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194296}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5503c223-e87a-5159-abb7-434053fd7b58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f754a120-8886-56d3-b535-398f13b91c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398529} {:answer/id #uuid "d28df103-ae23-5647-a506-1bc60c332868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398530} {:answer/id #uuid "e85142cb-e059-512c-8b7b-18eee7a8c253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398531} {:answer/id #uuid "e433762d-59a0-5efb-bef2-7687d8583f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398532} {:answer/id #uuid "3a53a3c7-e2f5-50e9-afd4-d3b986017cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u+v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e85142cb-e059-512c-8b7b-18eee7a8c253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398531} :answer-field/id #uuid "185487e5-090f-5815-93b2-dfc0c983e691" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3bcb9d3-050c-5ab9-bd2a-436465223147" :question/math-academy-id "q-161360" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,(u+v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}+2uv+{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2uv\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198379 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaa6b152-86d3-5f96-8a94-57f86a17a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Flux Over a Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1522d126-bc34-5af8-9b6a-e28d9a69cc28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275676} {:answer/id #uuid "18a12e63-447a-54f3-aa1b-7655d054b2a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275705} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0d9dd7-0a4c-53a0-93f3-266c540e5806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276630} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ec1fd9-ea87-51b3-9aac-bec86160b60b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277443} {:answer/id #uuid "eb954333-7f24-5dd3-958d-038c55f1b656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb954333-7f24-5dd3-958d-038c55f1b656" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277536} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b5f25c-b535-59ae-8da4-9392f8bb667d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "154ea74b-7c8a-5b64-880d-29244a657638" :question/math-academy-id "q-161382" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+y)=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+y)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y,g(x,y)) & =⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{z=2x+y} \\\\  & =⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xy(2x+y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{-x}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{-y}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{xy(2x+y)}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate our surface integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨-x,\\,-y,\\,xyz⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(-x)\\cdot 2-(-y)\\cdot (1)+xy(2x+y))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x+y+2{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+y+2{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2xy+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+\\frac{1}{2}+{x}^{2}+\\frac{x}{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{7x}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{x}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{7}{6}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198389 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Over a Surface as a Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002ddc9f-2c71-5478-8c1d-77a6a8c334bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275480} {:answer/id #uuid "023841e2-2821-56a0-955a-89084c15f8d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275496} {:answer/id #uuid "4d835b30-d2dd-53ba-9310-a5a2961e3b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u+2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276160} {:answer/id #uuid "b4df5cbd-8643-5942-bb9e-8d044eb77815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277092} {:answer/id #uuid "f42daa7a-2c08-5500-aa68-d0405d0dc904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3v+u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "002ddc9f-2c71-5478-8c1d-77a6a8c334bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275480} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca208624-88d6-5a85-8572-2dd062347b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06f1e075-9f39-52f0-b9b8-c179d2533ffc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161462" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,v+2(v-u),\\,2u-v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v-u,\\,3v-2u,\\,2u-v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(v-u)\\cdot 1+(3v-2u)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =v-u-3v+2u+2u-v \\\\  & =3u-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,y+2z,\\,2x-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(3u-3v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198392 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Over a Surface as a Repeated Integral Using a Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffab214-a531-5f16-9548-4aba64a14e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂z$ and $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401256} {:answer/id #uuid "27be7768-bf01-5a25-8f76-a7b3aa6827e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401257} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0b36ca-8d50-5d13-b2d4-01dff2d1189e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂y$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401258} {:answer/id #uuid "8c295efa-f53d-5757-9ea8-624ce01afe74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401259} {:answer/id #uuid "401f8a2b-7596-5052-8ec8-449369280a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂y$ and $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c295efa-f53d-5757-9ea8-624ce01afe74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401259} :answer-field/id #uuid "0585e533-2d5e-5fa5-b53e-85ce1c70e498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2128236-dd4e-5cec-8d28-c07554df0f5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161463" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{\\boxed{}}-Q\\frac{∂g}{\\boxed{}}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
